==include xmodem.cif

==name ymodem

==short-description

An implementation of the YMODEM file transfer protocol.

==long-description

Allows the transfer of files to and from remote terminal software that supports YMODEM. Supports batch mode, allowing multiple files to be sent and received. Filenames use strict UTF-8 block-zero metadata; file data remains binary. The native RFile size limit is 2,147,483,647 bytes; larger advertised files are rejected. Note, the console implementation that ymodem is attached to must support binary mode. If it doesn't, C<KErrExtensionNotSupported> (-47) will be reported. In practice, this currently means that one of the vt100 console variants (F<vt100cons.dll>, F<vt100busdevcons.dll>, F<vt100usbcons.dll>, F<vt100btcons.dll> or F<vt100tcpcons.dll>) must be used.

Note, when sending, file names specified with wild characters are accepted. When receiving, specify a directory into which one or more files should be received. If no directory is specified, the received files will be saved in the current working directory (the name of each received file is provided by the sending end).

==option filename O output

Receive a single file to this exact destination. Existing destinations require --overwrite. Input is written to a sibling temporary file, flushed and finalized only after complete reception.

==option string H sha256

Expected SHA-256 hexadecimal digest for a single received file. With a crypto-enabled build, verify the digest before finalizing the destination. A mismatch fails and preserves any existing destination.

==argument filename file_name optional multiple

==see-also

L<xmodem|xmodem>

